sections.content:
**Path 1: Java Agent (easiest, zero-code)**

Download the agent and launch with:

```bash
java -javaagent:opentelemetry-javaagent.jar \
  -Dotel.service.name=payment-service \
  -Dotel.exporter.otlp.endpoint=http://otel-collector:4318 \
  -jar app.jar
```

The agent auto-instruments Spring MVC, Spring WebFlux, JDBC, Apache HTTP Client, OkHttp, Kafka, Redis, MongoDB, and 100+ other libraries. You get HTTP spans, DB spans, messaging spans with no code changes.

Environment variables for configuration:
- `OTEL_SERVICE_NAME=payment-service`
- `OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT=http://collector:4318`
- `OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_PROTOCOL=http/protobuf` or `grpc`
- `OTEL_RESOURCE_ATTRIBUTES=env=production,team=payments`
- `OTEL_TRACES_SAMPLER=parentbased_traceidratio`
- `OTEL_TRACES_SAMPLER_ARG=0.1` (10% sampling)

**Path 2: Spring Boot Starter (more control, still easy)**

```xml
<dependency>
  <groupId>io.opentelemetry.instrumentation</groupId>
  <artifactId>opentelemetry-spring-boot-starter</artifactId>
  <version>2.10.0</version>
</dependency>
```

Application properties:

```yaml
otel:
  service:
    name: payment-service
  exporter:
    otlp:
      endpoint: http://otel-collector:4318
      protocol: http/protobuf
  resource:
    attributes: env=production,team=payments
  traces:
    sampler: parentbased_traceidratio
    sampler.arg: 0.1
```

Starter uses Spring's auto-config; works well with Spring Boot's Actuator and Micrometer.

**Path 3: Manual SDK (most control)**

```java
@Configuration
public class OtelConfig {
    @Bean
    public OpenTelemetry openTelemetry() {
        Resource resource = Resource.getDefault()
            .merge(Resource.create(Attributes.of(
                AttributeKey.stringKey("service.name"), "payment-service")));
        SdkTracerProvider tracerProvider = SdkTracerProvider.builder()
            .addSpanProcessor(BatchSpanProcessor.builder(
                OtlpHttpSpanExporter.builder()
                    .setEndpoint("http://otel-collector:4318/v1/traces")
                    .build()).build())
            .setResource(resource)
            .build();
        return OpenTelemetrySdk.builder()
            .setTracerProvider(tracerProvider)
            .setPropagators(ContextPropagators.create(W3CTraceContextPropagator.getInstance()))
            .buildAndRegisterGlobal();
    }
}
```

**Manual instrumentation for business spans:**

```java
@Service
public class PaymentService {
    private static final Tracer tracer = GlobalOpenTelemetry.getTracer("payment-service");

    public PaymentResult charge(Payment payment) {
        Span span = tracer.spanBuilder("payment.charge")
            .setAttribute("payment.id", payment.getId())
            .setAttribute("payment.amount", payment.getAmount())
            .setAttribute("payment.currency", payment.getCurrency())
            .setSpanKind(SpanKind.INTERNAL)
            .startSpan();
        try (Scope scope = span.makeCurrent()) {
            PaymentResult result = processInternal(payment);
            span.setAttribute("payment.status", result.getStatus());
            return result;
        } catch (Exception e) {
            span.recordException(e);
            span.setStatus(StatusCode.ERROR, e.getMessage());
            throw e;
        } finally {
            span.end();
        }
    }
}
```

**Metrics with Meter API:**

```java
Meter meter = GlobalOpenTelemetry.getMeter("payment-service");
LongCounter paymentCounter = meter.counterBuilder("payments.processed")
    .setDescription("Number of payments processed")
    .setUnit("payments")
    .build();
paymentCounter.add(1, Attributes.of(AttributeKey.stringKey("status"), "success"));
```
